NV_PK(20,{"the main ingredient is pork intestine or pork stomach it must be washed very clean and then stewed with the herbs until soft just before serving the owner adds a few drops of angelica rice wine and the smell rises at once":"","four herb soup goes best with gua bao zongzi and sticky rice at luo cheng and hao nong jia in tainan or yuan fang in taipei you can order a bowl to go with your meal":"","the soup was first called four ministers soup in taiwanese the words for minister and god sound alike so the name became four gods soup":"","one four herb soup please":"","a few drops of rice wine please":"","lotus seed":"","the small white seed of the lotus plant used in soups and desserts":"","lotus seeds are soft after cooking":"","intestine":"","the long tube inside the body that food passes through":"","pork intestine must be washed very well":"","gentle":"","soft and mild not strong":"","the soup has a gentle taste":"","a very small amount of liquid":"","add a few drops of rice wine":"","first a lot of chinese cabbage is cooked in pork bone broth until it is very soft then a whole duck goes in and cooks for about three hours the flavor comes from garlic dried flatfish and fried shallots and the soup is sweet and fragrant":"","dried flatfish is often used in taiwanese cooking to make soup more fragrant":""});